freetype: take the font, text color and outline color while text shows

A player that changes freetype-font or freetype-outline-color while it
plays (through libvlc_media_player_set_filter_option(), patches/0001) never
saw the change: FillDefaultStyles() reads them once, when the text renderer
is created, while UpdateDefaultLiveStyles(), run before every Render(),
re-reads only the text color, background and outline thickness.

Read the outline color and the font family there too, and reload the
default face when the family changed, as Render() already does when the
size changes. Lines rendered after the change take it.

Carried by Ferricone Player on top of VLC a5538c55; written for upstream.

diff --git i/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c w/modules/text_renderer/freetype/freetype.c
